# A causal loop: CTA c runs c trips, so the count is %ctaid.x and the
# guard skipping CTA 0 is the loop's entry. Per CTA the totals are
# exact in %ctaid.x; over the launch each CTA's threads count its
# trips, 0 + 1 + 2 + 3, so the barrier runs 192 times with 4 CTAs.
# Without the guard CTA 0 runs once, the count is max(%ctaid.x, 1), and
# its sum over the grid, 7, gives 224 barriers
# (micro/cta_trips.unguarded.ncu.json).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-REC "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=REC "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.unguarded.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-SUM "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.unguarded.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=SUM "%s"
ANN-FREE: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips %ctaid.x | warp * × lane * | under line 30 | exec 32·%ctaid.x/CTA{{$}}
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: bar.sync{{ +}}32 * %ctaid.x{{ +}}%ctaid.x{{$}}
ANN-REC: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips %ctaid.x | warp * × lane * | CTAs %ctaid.x ≥ 1 (3/4) | exec 192/launch{{$}}
REC: totals per launch [static]:
REC: bar.sync{{ +}}192{{ +}}6{{$}}
ANN-SUM: {{^}}$L__BB1_1: // loop: trips max(%ctaid.x, 1) | warp * × lane * | exec 224/launch{{$}}
SUM-LABEL: kernel micro_cta_trips_unguarded
SUM: totals per launch [static]:
SUM: bar.sync{{ +}}224{{ +}}7{{$}}
